{"id":"torrey:manna","source":"torrey","name":"Manna","slug":"manna","seeAlso":[],"entries":[{"text":"Miraculously given to Israel for food in the wilderness — Ex 16:4,15; Ne 9:15.","refs":[["Exod",16,4,16,4],["Exod",16,15,16,15],["Neh",9,15,9,15]]},{"text":"God’s manna. — Ne 9:20.","refs":[["Neh",9,20,9,20]]},{"text":"Bread of heaven. — Ps 105:40.","refs":[["Ps",105,40,105,40]]},{"text":"Bread from heaven. — Ex 16:4; Joh 6:31.","refs":[["Exod",16,4,16,4],["John",6,31,6,31]]},{"text":"Corn of heaven. — Ps 78:24.","refs":[["Ps",78,24,78,24]]},{"text":"Angel’s food. — Ps 78:25.","refs":[["Ps",78,25,78,25]]},{"text":"Spiritual meat. — 1Co 10:3.","refs":[["1Cor",10,3,10,3]]},{"text":"Previously unknown — De 8:3,16.","refs":[["Deut",8,3,8,3],["Deut",8,16,8,16]]},{"text":"Like coriander seed. — Ex 16:31; Nu 11:7.","refs":[["Exod",16,31,16,31],["Num",11,7,11,7]]},{"text":"White. — Ex 16:31.","refs":[["Exod",16,31,16,31]]},{"text":"Like in colour to bdellium. — Nu 11:7.","refs":[["Num",11,7,11,7]]},{"text":"Like in taste to wafers made with honey. — Ex 16:31.","refs":[["Exod",16,31,16,31]]},{"text":"Like in taste to oil. — Nu 11:18.","refs":[["Num",11,18,11,18]]},{"text":"Like hoar frost. — Ex 16:14.","refs":[["Exod",16,14,16,14]]},{"text":"Fell after the evening dew — Nu 11:9.","refs":[["Num",11,9,11,9]]},{"text":"None fell on the Sabbath day — Ex 16:26,27.","refs":[["Exod",16,26,16,26],["Exod",16,27,16,27]]},{"text":"Gathered every morning — Ex 16:21.","refs":[["Exod",16,21,16,21]]},{"text":"An omer of, gathered for each person — Ex 16:16.","refs":[["Exod",16,16,16,16]]},{"text":"Two portions of, gathered the sixth day on account of the Sabbath — Ex 16:5,22-26.","refs":[["Exod",16,5,16,5],["Exod",16,22,16,26]]},{"text":"He that gathered much or little had sufficient and nothing over — Ex 16:18.","refs":[["Exod",16,18,16,18]]},{"text":"Melted away by the sun — Ex 16:21.","refs":[["Exod",16,21,16,21]]},{"text":"When Israel murmured for bread. — Ex 16:2,3.","refs":[["Exod",16,2,16,2],["Exod",16,3,16,3]]},{"text":"In answer to prayer. — Ps 105:40.","refs":[["Ps",105,40,105,40]]},{"text":"Through Moses. — Joh 6:31,32.","refs":[["John",6,31,6,31],["John",6,32,6,32]]},{"text":"To exhibit God’s glory. — Ex 16:7.","refs":[["Exod",16,7,16,7]]},{"text":"As a sign of Moses’s divine mission. — Joh 6:30,31.","refs":[["John",6,30,6,30],["John",6,31,6,31]]},{"text":"For forty years. — Ne 9:21.","refs":[["Neh",9,21,9,21]]},{"text":"As a test of obedience. — Ex 16:4.","refs":[["Exod",16,4,16,4]]},{"text":"To teach that man does not live by bread only. — De 8:3; Mt 4:4.","refs":[["Deut",8,3,8,3],["Matt",4,4,4,4]]},{"text":"To humble and prove Israel. — De 8:16.","refs":[["Deut",8,16,8,16]]},{"text":"Kept longer than a day (except on the Sabbath) became corrupt — Ex 16:19,20.","refs":[["Exod",16,19,16,19],["Exod",16,20,16,20]]},{"text":"At first covetous of. — Ex 16:17.","refs":[["Exod",16,17,16,17]]},{"text":"Ground, made into cakes and baked in pans. — Nu 11:8.","refs":[["Num",11,8,11,8]]},{"text":"Counted inferior to food of Egypt. — Nu 11:4-6.","refs":[["Num",11,4,11,6]]},{"text":"Loathed. — Nu 21:5.","refs":[["Num",21,5,21,5]]},{"text":"Punished for despising. — Nu 11:10-20.","refs":[["Num",11,10,11,20]]},{"text":"Punished for loathing. — Nu 21:6.","refs":[["Num",21,6,21,6]]},{"text":"Ceased when Israel entered Canaan — Ex 16:35; Jos 5:12.","refs":[["Exod",16,35,16,35],["Josh",5,12,5,12]]},{"text":"Christ. — Joh 6:32-35.","refs":[["John",6,32,6,35]]},{"text":"Blessedness given to saints. — Re 2:17.","refs":[["Rev",2,17,2,17]]},{"text":"A golden pot of, laid up in the holiest for a memorial — Ex 16:32-34; Heb 9:4.","refs":[["Exod",16,32,16,34],["Heb",9,4,9,4]]}],"refCount":55}
